# Component Patterns

## Component Structure

### Standard Component Template

```tsx
import React from "react";

interface ComponentNameProps {
  children?: React.ReactNode;
  className?: string;
  // Other specific props
}

const ComponentName: React.FC<ComponentNameProps> = ({
  children,
  className = "",
  // Other props with defaults
}) => {
  return <div className={`base-classes ${className}`}>{children}</div>;
};

export default ComponentName;
```

## Interactive Components

### Button Components with Hover Effects

Reference: [CTAButton.tsx](mdc:src/components/atoms/CTAButton.tsx)

```tsx
// Add proper hover states and transitions
className="transition-all hover:bg-gray-800"

// For complex interactions, use group patterns
<button className="group">
  <div className="opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-10" />
</button>
```

## Layout Patterns

### Header Layout

Reference: [header.tsx](mdc:src/layouts/header.tsx)

Key patterns:

- Fixed height: `h-16`
- Backdrop blur: `backdrop-blur-3xl`
- Container with responsive padding
- Mobile-first navigation (hide menu on mobile)

### Section Layout

Reference: [HeroSection.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/HeroSection.tsx)

Key patterns:

- Calculate height minus header: `h-[calc(100vh-4rem)]`
- Two-column responsive layout: `lg:flex-row lg:w-1/2`
- Aspect ratio for media: `aspect-video`

## Responsive Patterns

### Mobile-First Approach

```tsx
// Hide on mobile, show on tablet+
<div className="hidden md:block">
  <NavigationMenu />
</div>

// Stack on mobile, row on larger screens
<div className="flex flex-col lg:flex-row">
  <div className="w-full lg:w-1/2">Left</div>
  <div className="w-full lg:w-1/2">Right</div>
</div>
```

### Button Groups

```tsx
// Stack on mobile, row on small screens+
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6">
  <CTAButton>Primary</CTAButton>
  <CTAButton>Secondary</CTAButton>
</div>
```

## Typography Patterns

### Responsive Text Sizing

```tsx
// Progressive sizing with breakpoints
className = "text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl xl:text-6xl";

// Consistent line heights
className = "leading-tight"; // for headings
className = "leading-relaxed"; // for body text
```

## Import Patterns

### Path Aliases

Always use `@/` path alias for internal imports:

```tsx
import ComponentName from "@/components/atoms/ComponentName";
import { utilFunction } from "@/lib/utils";
```

### Import Organization

1. React imports first
2. External library imports
3. Internal component imports (atoms → molecules → organisms)
4. Utility imports last
